  "title": "Bluetooth speaker experiment (14 subjects, 6 classes, 31 EEG ch)",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 14 healthy participants performing a visual P300 oddball brain-computer interface task for controlling a Bluetooth speaker, one of several home appliances. Six stimulus classes were presented on an LCD display, and 31-channel EEG was recorded at 500 Hz. The dataset supports research on ERP-based BCIs for home appliance control and inter-subject transfer learning.",
  "methods_description": "31-channel EEG was recorded with an actiCHamp active-electrode system (Brain Products) at 500 Hz, referenced to linked mastoids, using a standard 10-20 montage. Visual flash stimuli were shown on an LCD display with a 750 ms stimulus onset asynchrony. Each subject completed 50 training and 30 testing blocks in one session, with online visual feedback.",
